  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Summary\nThe `UnstakeMessenger.unstake()` function is designed to support a buffered-fee flow via helper quote functions, but the underlying LayerZero `OAppSender._payNative()` implementation enforces strict equality between `msg.value` and the quoted fee. When callers use the buffered-fee helper and send more than the exact quoted amount, all unstake calls revert with `NotEnoughNative`.\n\n### Description\nThe cross-chain unstake entrypoint on the spoke chain is `UnstakeMessenger.unstake(uint256 returnTripAllocation)`. Its high-level flow is:\n\n1. Build an unstake payload that encodes `msg.sender` as the user.\n2. Compute the LayerZero fee via `_quote(hubEid, payload, options, false)`, which returns a `MessagingFee` fee with `fee.nativeFee` set to the exact required amount.\n3. Enforce `msg.value >= fee.nativeFee`, reverting with `InsufficientFee(fee.nativeFee, msg.value)` if the caller underpays.\n4. Call `_lzSend(hubEid, payload, options, fee, payable(msg.sender))`, passing the exact fee struct to the LayerZero endpoint.\n\nTo make integration safer, `UnstakeMessenger` also exposes buffered-fee helpers such as `quoteUnstakeWithBuffer()`. These helpers deliberately return a fee that is larger than the exact LayerZero quote (for example, exactFee * 110 / 100) so that integrators can:\n\n1. Call `quoteUnstakeWithBuffer()` to obtain a buffered fee.\n2. Call `unstake{value: bufferedFee}(returnTripAllocation)` and rely on the refund address for any excess.\n\nHowever, the inherited LayerZero implementation for `_payNative()` (used inside _lzSend()) requires that `msg.value` equals the native fee exactly:\n```solidity\nfunction _payNative(uint256 _nativeFee) internal virtual returns (uint256 nativeFee) {\n    if (msg.value != _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value);\n    return _nativeFee;\n}\n```\nBecause `UnstakeMessenger.unstake()` passes `fee.nativeFee` (the exact quoted amount) into `_lzSend()`, but the caller may send `msg.value > fee.nativeFee` when using the buffered helper, `_payNative()` observes the mismatch and reverts with `NotEnoughNative(msg.value)` before the message is dispatched.\n\nThis behavior was confirmed via tests that:\n\n- Succeed when msg.value == exactFee returned by quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue().\n- Revert when msg.value == bufferedFee returned by quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() (10% higher than exactFee), with selector OAppSender.NotEnoughNative(uint256).\n- Revert even when msg.value == exactFee + 1 wei.\n\nAs a result, the “buffered fee” integration pattern exposed by the contract is unusable in practice.\n\nWhen integrators follow the buffered-fee pattern provided by `UnstakeMessenger` (calling the buffer quote helper and forwarding that value as msg.value), all cross-chain `unstake()` calls revert before any LayerZero message is sent. Users cannot complete cross-chain unstake operations via the buffered flow, and integrators must instead rely on exact-fee quoting, which is more fragile to timing and gas-price changes between quote and execution. The issue does not directly cause fund loss, but it breaks a primary cross-chain unstake UX path and can lead to persistent user-facing failures until the integration is adjusted.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nConsider aligning the `UnstakeMessenger` implementation with the intended buffered-fee behavior so that overpayment is accepted and excess is refunded rather than causing a revert. Possible approaches include:\n\n- Overriding `_payNative()` in `UnstakeMessenger` (or a derived helper) to accept `msg.value >= _nativeFee`, forward only `_nativeFee` to the endpoint, and refund any excess directly to msg.sender before calling endpoint.send. This keeps the LayerZero integration local to this contract and makes buffered-fee usage safe.\n- Alternatively, adjusting `unstake()` so that `_lzSend()` is called with `_nativeFee = msg.value` after validating `msg.value >= fee.nativeFee`, and relying on the endpoint’s refund mechanism for any unused amount, ensuring `_payNative()` sees `_nativeFee == msg.value`.\n\nIn either case, it would be beneficial to update comments and any external integration docs to clearly describe the expected fee patterns (exact vs buffered) so that integrators use the supported flow.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.19;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {UnstakeMessenger} from \"../src/token/wiTRY/crosschain/UnstakeMessenger.sol\";\nimport {IUnstakeMessenger} from \"../src/token/wiTRY/crosschain/interfaces/IUnstakeMessenger.sol\";\nimport {OAppSender} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-oapp-v2/contracts/oapp/OAppSender.sol\";\nimport {MessagingFee, MessagingReceipt} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-oapp-v2/contracts/oapp/OAppSender.sol\";\nimport {MessagingParams} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-protocol-v2/contracts/interfaces/ILayerZeroEndpointV2.sol\";\nimport {OptionsBuilder} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-oapp-v2/contracts/oapp/libs/OptionsBuilder.sol\";\nimport {EnforcedOptionParam} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-oapp-v2/contracts/oapp/interfaces/IOAppOptionsType3.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title RealisticMockLayerZeroEndpoint\n * @notice A mock LayerZero endpoint that properly validates msg.value\n * @dev The actual LayerZero endpoint.send() expects to receive exactly the quoted fee.\n *      The issue is that _payNative() in OAppSender checks msg.value == _nativeFee,\n *      but UnstakeMessenger allows msg.value >= fee.nativeFee before calling _lzSend.\n */\ncontract RealisticMockLayerZeroEndpoint {\n    uint64 public nonce;\n    uint256 public quotedNativeFee;\n    uint256 public quotedLzTokenFee;\n    bytes32 public lastGuid;\n\n    // Track last send call\n    uint32 public lastDstEid;\n    bytes public lastPayload;\n    bytes public lastOptions;\n    MessagingFee public lastFee;\n    address public lastRefundAddress;\n\n    // Track delegate\n    address public delegate;\n\n    function setDelegate(address _delegate) external {\n        delegate = _delegate;\n    }\n\n    function setQuote(uint256 nativeFee, uint256 lzTokenFee) external {\n        quotedNativeFee = nativeFee;\n        quotedLzTokenFee = lzTokenFee;\n    }\n\n    function quote(MessagingParams calldata, address) external view returns (MessagingFee memory) {\n        return MessagingFee(quotedNativeFee, quotedLzTokenFee);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice The send function that the endpoint calls\n     * @dev In the real LayerZero implementation, this receives the exact fee amount\n     *      because _payNative() only returns _nativeFee (after validating msg.value == _nativeFee).\n     *      However, the actual issue occurs BEFORE this - in _payNative() inside OAppSender.\n     */\n    function send(MessagingParams calldata _params, address _refundAddress)\n        external\n        payable\n        returns (MessagingReceipt memory)\n    {\n        // The endpoint receives whatever value is sent\n        // In practice, this is _nativeFee from _payNative()\n        lastDstEid = _params.dstEid;\n        lastPayload = _params.message;\n        lastOptions = _params.options;\n        lastFee = MessagingFee(msg.value, 0);\n        lastRefundAddress = _refundAddress;\n\n        nonce++;\n        lastGuid = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(_params.dstEid, nonce));\n\n        return MessagingReceipt(lastGuid, nonce, MessagingFee(msg.value, 0));\n    }\n\n    function getLastSendParams()\n        external\n        view\n        returns (\n            uint32 dstEid,\n            bytes memory payload,\n            bytes memory options,\n            MessagingFee memory fee,\n            address refundAddress\n        )\n    {\n        return (lastDstEid, lastPayload, lastOptions, lastFee, lastRefundAddress);\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * @title BufferedFeeRevertPoC\n * @notice Proof of Concept: Buffered-fee cross-chain unstake reverts due to strict native fee equality\n *\n * FINDING SUMMARY:\n * ----------------\n * The UnstakeMessenger.unstake() function allows msg.value >= fee.nativeFee, but the underlying\n * LayerZero OAppSender._payNative() enforces strict equality: msg.value == _nativeFee.\n *\n * When users call quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() and send the buffered fee (e.g., 10% extra),\n * the transaction reverts with NotEnoughNative(msg.value) because:\n *   1. UnstakeMessenger.unstake() passes fee.nativeFee (exact quote) to _lzSend()\n *   2. _lzSend() calls _payNative(fee.nativeFee)\n *   3. _payNative() checks: if (msg.value != _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value)\n *   4. Since msg.value > fee.nativeFee (due to buffer), the check fails\n *\n * IMPACT:\n * -------\n *   - The \"buffered fee\" integration pattern exposed by UnstakeMessenger is unusable\n *   - Users following the documented pattern will have all unstake() calls revert\n *   - Integrators must use exact-fee quoting, which is fragile to timing/gas-price changes\n */\ncontract BufferedFeeRevertPoC is Test {\n    using OptionsBuilder for bytes;\n\n    UnstakeMessenger public messenger;\n    RealisticMockLayerZeroEndpoint public mockEndpoint;\n\n    address public owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n    address public user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n    uint32 public hubEid = 40161; // Sepolia\n\n    bytes32 public hubPeer = bytes32(uint256(uint160(makeAddr(\"hubVaultComposer\"))));\n\n    // Constants\n    uint16 constant MSG_TYPE_UNSTAKE = 1;\n    uint128 constant LZ_RECEIVE_GAS = 350000;\n    uint256 constant BPS_DENOMINATOR = 10000;\n    uint256 constant USER_INITIAL_BALANCE = 100 ether;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy mock endpoint\n        mockEndpoint = new RealisticMockLayerZeroEndpoint();\n\n        // Deploy UnstakeMessenger\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        messenger = new UnstakeMessenger(address(mockEndpoint), owner, hubEid);\n\n        // Configure hub peer\n        messenger.setPeer(hubEid, hubPeer);\n\n        // Setup enforced options (matching production config)\n        EnforcedOptionParam[] memory params = new EnforcedOptionParam[](1);\n        bytes memory enforced = OptionsBuilder.newOptions().addExecutorLzReceiveOption(LZ_RECEIVE_GAS, 0);\n        params[0] = EnforcedOptionParam({eid: hubEid, msgType: MSG_TYPE_UNSTAKE, options: enforced});\n        messenger.setEnforcedOptions(params);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Fund user\n        vm.deal(user, USER_INITIAL_BALANCE);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice PoC: Exact fee works correctly\n     * @dev This test demonstrates the expected behavior when using exact fee\n     */\n    function test_exactFee_succeeds() public {\n        console.log(\"=== TEST: Exact Fee Works Correctly ===\");\n\n        // Set up mock quote\n        uint256 baseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(baseFee, 0);\n\n        // Get exact quote\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.001 ether;\n        (uint256 exactFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        console.log(\"Exact fee quoted:\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"User sends msg.value:\", exactFee);\n\n        // Execute unstake with exact fee - should succeed\n        vm.prank(user);\n        bytes32 guid = messenger.unstake{value: exactFee}(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        assertTrue(guid != bytes32(0), \"Unstake should succeed with exact fee\");\n        console.log(\"SUCCESS: Unstake completed with GUID:\", vm.toString(guid));\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice PoC: Buffered fee causes revert\n     * @dev This is the core vulnerability demonstration\n     *\n     * The buffered fee helper quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() returns exactFee * 1.10 (10% buffer).\n     * When the user sends this buffered amount as msg.value, the transaction reverts because:\n     *\n     * In OAppSender._payNative():\n     *   function _payNative(uint256 _nativeFee) internal virtual returns (uint256 nativeFee) {\n     *       if (msg.value != _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value);\n     *       return _nativeFee;\n     *   }\n     *\n     * The _nativeFee passed is fee.nativeFee (the exact quote), but msg.value is the buffered amount.\n     * Since msg.value > _nativeFee, the equality check fails and reverts.\n     */\n    function test_PoC_bufferedFee_reverts() public {\n        console.log(\"=== PoC: Buffered Fee Causes Revert ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // Set up mock quote\n        uint256 baseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(baseFee, 0);\n\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.001 ether;\n\n        // Get both exact and buffered quotes\n        (uint256 exactFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue(returnTripAllocation);\n        (uint256 bufferedFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithBuffer(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        console.log(\"Step 1: Quote Fees\");\n        console.log(\"  - Exact fee (quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue):\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffered fee (quoteUnstakeWithBuffer):\", bufferedFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffer amount:\", bufferedFee - exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffer percentage:\", (bufferedFee - exactFee) * 100 / exactFee, \"%\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        console.log(\"Step 2: User follows documented buffered-fee pattern\");\n        console.log(\"  - User calls quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() to get recommended fee\");\n        console.log(\"  - User sends msg.value =\", bufferedFee);\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        console.log(\"Step 3: Transaction execution\");\n        console.log(\"  - UnstakeMessenger.unstake() checks: msg.value >= fee.nativeFee\");\n        console.log(\"  - Check passes:\", bufferedFee, \">=\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - UnstakeMessenger calls _lzSend() with fee.nativeFee =\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        console.log(\"Step 4: OAppSender._payNative() is called\");\n        console.log(\"  - _payNative receives _nativeFee =\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - _payNative checks: msg.value == _nativeFee\");\n        console.log(\"  - Check: bufferedFee == exactFee ?\");\n        console.log(\"   \", bufferedFee, \"==\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Result: FALSE - will revert!\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // Execute and expect revert\n        console.log(\"Step 5: Attempting unstake with buffered fee...\");\n\n        // The revert happens in _payNative() with NotEnoughNative(msg.value)\n        // Note: The error is named NotEnoughNative but it's actually checking for EXACT equality\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(OAppSender.NotEnoughNative.selector, bufferedFee));\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        messenger.unstake{value: bufferedFee}(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        // This line is never reached due to revert\n        console.log(\"UNREACHABLE\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice PoC: Even 1 wei extra causes revert\n     * @dev Demonstrates that ANY overpayment causes failure, not just large buffers\n     */\n    function test_PoC_oneWeiExtra_reverts() public {\n        console.log(\"=== PoC: Even 1 Wei Extra Causes Revert ===\");\n\n        uint256 baseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(baseFee, 0);\n\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.001 ether;\n        (uint256 exactFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        uint256 exactFeePlusOne = exactFee + 1;\n\n        console.log(\"Exact fee:\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"Sending:\", exactFeePlusOne, \"(exact + 1 wei)\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(OAppSender.NotEnoughNative.selector, exactFeePlusOne));\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        messenger.unstake{value: exactFeePlusOne}(returnTripAllocation);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Demonstrates the intended use case that is broken\n     * @dev The contract explicitly provides quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() for safety,\n     *      but using it causes all transactions to revert\n     */\n    function test_PoC_intendedSafetyPatternBroken() public {\n        console.log(\"=== PoC: Intended Safety Pattern is Broken ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"INTENDED USAGE (from contract comments):\");\n        console.log(\"1. Call quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() to get fee with safety margin\");\n        console.log(\"2. Send that fee as msg.value to unstake()\");\n        console.log(\"3. Contract uses exact fees; excess buffer refunded to user\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"ACTUAL BEHAVIOR:\");\n        console.log(\"Transaction reverts before any refund can occur!\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        uint256 baseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(baseFee, 0);\n\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.001 ether;\n\n        // Following the documented pattern\n        (uint256 recommendedFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithBuffer(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        console.log(\"Following documented pattern:\");\n        console.log(\"  - quoteUnstakeWithBuffer() returns:\", recommendedFee);\n        console.log(\"  - User sends msg.value:\", recommendedFee);\n        console.log(\"\");\n\n        // This should work according to the docs, but it reverts\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(OAppSender.NotEnoughNative.selector, recommendedFee));\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        messenger.unstake{value: recommendedFee}(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        console.log(\"RESULT: Reverted with NotEnoughNative even though msg.value > required fee\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Shows the root cause in the code flow\n     */\n    function test_explainRootCause() public pure {\n        console.log(\"=== ROOT CAUSE EXPLANATION ===\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"UnstakeMessenger.unstake() at line 134:\");\n        console.log(\"  if (msg.value < fee.nativeFee) revert InsufficientFee(...)\");\n        console.log(\"  // This allows msg.value >= fee.nativeFee (overpayment OK)\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"UnstakeMessenger.unstake() at line 139-145:\");\n        console.log(\"  MessagingReceipt memory receipt = _lzSend(\");\n        console.log(\"      hubEid,\");\n        console.log(\"      payload,\");\n        console.log(\"      options,\");\n        console.log(\"      fee,  // <-- passes the EXACT quoted fee struct\");\n        console.log(\"      payable(msg.sender)\");\n        console.log(\"  );\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"OAppSender._lzSend() at line 82:\");\n        console.log(\"  uint256 messageValue = _payNative(_fee.nativeFee);\");\n        console.log(\"  // <-- passes _fee.nativeFee (exact quote)\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"OAppSender._payNative() at line 104-107:\");\n        console.log(\"  function _payNative(uint256 _nativeFee) internal virtual returns (uint256) {\");\n        console.log(\"      if (msg.value != _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value);\");\n        console.log(\"      // <-- STRICT EQUALITY check causes revert\");\n        console.log(\"      return _nativeFee;\");\n        console.log(\"  }\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"MISMATCH:\");\n        console.log(\"  - UnstakeMessenger allows: msg.value >= fee.nativeFee\");\n        console.log(\"  - OAppSender requires:     msg.value == fee.nativeFee\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"RESULT: Overpayment (buffer) causes revert in _payNative()\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Confirms the documented fee buffer helpers exist but are unusable\n     */\n    function test_feeBufferHelperExists() public {\n        // Set up a realistic quote\n        uint256 baseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(baseFee, 0);\n\n        // Verify the buffer helper exists and returns a higher value\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.001 ether;\n\n        (uint256 exactFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue(returnTripAllocation);\n        (uint256 bufferedFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithBuffer(returnTripAllocation);\n\n        // Buffer is 10% (1000 BPS) by default\n        uint256 expectedBuffer = messenger.feeBufferBPS();\n        uint256 expectedBufferedFee = (exactFee * (BPS_DENOMINATOR + expectedBuffer)) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;\n\n        assertEq(bufferedFee, expectedBufferedFee, \"Buffer calculation is correct\");\n        assertGt(bufferedFee, exactFee, \"Buffered fee is greater than exact fee\");\n\n        console.log(\"Fee buffer helper exists and calculates correctly:\");\n        console.log(\"  - Exact fee:\", exactFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffered fee:\", bufferedFee);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffer BPS:\", expectedBuffer);\n        console.log(\"  - Buffer percentage:\", expectedBuffer / 100, \"%\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"But using the buffered fee causes revert!\");\n    }\n}\n```",
